<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="Page-1" id="NtHRcTd-8NjwkrXfjE-V">
    <mxGraphModel dx="4146" dy="2639" grid="1" gridSize="12.5" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="3600" pageHeight="2400" background="light-dark(#FFFFFF,#121212)" math="1" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="p-YKAdcl-ozBapOeaQL1-12" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;spacingLeft=0;spacingTop=0;spacing=50;fontFamily=Poppins;fillColor=default;strokeColor=default;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="587.5" width="1400" x="1100" y="1712.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2W8dqJh8dfOg5UK6-tmS-2" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeColor=#d79b00;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Poppins;fontSize=130;fontColor=#FFFFFF;labelBackgroundColor=none;horizontal=1;autosizeText=0;fillColor=#7A003C;gradientColor=none;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="400" width="3400" x="100" y="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="X6AeTYXP2CFdlURwPi2P-12" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;spacingLeft=0;spacingTop=0;spacing=50;fontFamily=Poppins;fillColor=default;strokeColor=default;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 44px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font&gt;What Is GOOL?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;GOOL, the Generic Object-Oriented Language, is a language that is generic over mainstream object-oriented languages [1]. GOOL takes a &quot;write once, generate everywhere&quot; approach, meaning that a program written in GOOL can initially translated to one language, then translated to another language with few or no changes if the first language is found lacking.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="500" width="900" x="100" y="600" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="X6AeTYXP2CFdlURwPi2P-13" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;spacingLeft=0;spacingTop=0;spacing=50;fontFamily=Poppins;fillColor=default;strokeColor=default;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 44px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Program Organization&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;All mainstream languages have some mechanism for organizing a piece of software and managing visibility of names. This usually involves a tree of directory-like things and file-like&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt; things. There are many differences between languages, however, e.g.:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;Java: packages with public/private, no subpackages [2]&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;C#: namespaces with public/private, with nested namespaces&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;Swift: modules (i.e. files) with visibility management&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;Python, Julia: packages represented as files, no visibility management options&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;Rust: modules and submodules&lt;br&gt;(usually folders and subfolders)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;… etc. Every language has its quirks.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Problem&lt;/b&gt;: current GOOL doesn&#39;t know about these&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt; differences!&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;It assumes that a program is simply a list of files, with no other nuances.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1100" width="900" x="100" y="1200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2W8dqJh8dfOg5UK6-tmS-3" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;horizontal=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;autosizeText=0;fontSize=50;labelBackgroundColor=none;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontFamily=Poppins;" value="&lt;u&gt;&lt;b&gt;Brandon Bosman&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/u&gt;, Dr. Jacques Carette&lt;br&gt;Department of Computing and Software, McMaster University" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="208.03" width="2237.5" x="450" y="291.97" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2W8dqJh8dfOg5UK6-tmS-5" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;editableCssRules=.*;image=data:image/svg+xml,;fontFamily=Poppins;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="204.94" width="765.79" x="2687.5" y="189.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2W8dqJh8dfOg5UK6-tmS-6" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;fontFamily=Poppins;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="300" width="300" x="150" y="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="X6AeTYXP2CFdlURwPi2P-3" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;horizontal=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;autosizeText=0;fontSize=85;labelBackgroundColor=none;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontFamily=Poppins;" value="A Generic Representation of Program Organization" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="225" width="2237.5" x="450" y="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="U_MLOzHVXz4xIFYg9_O6-2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;spacingLeft=0;spacingTop=0;spacing=50;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;fontFamily=Poppins;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 44px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font&gt;Generically Representing Program Organization in GOOL&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;GOOL aims to be a &quot;write once, generate everywhere&quot; language: one GOOL program should be usable in generating a host of idiomatic code in a variety of desired languages, with no language-specific concerns. This requires a generic representation of program organization that maps onto each language&#39;s own structures.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;I need to put something here...&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1012.5" width="1400" x="1100" y="600" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="U_MLOzHVXz4xIFYg9_O6-3" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;spacingLeft=0;spacingTop=0;spacing=50;fontFamily=Poppins;fillColor=default;strokeColor=default;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 44px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font&gt;References&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font&gt;[1] Carette, J., MacLachlan, B., Smith, S. (2020). GOOL: A Generic Object-Oriented Language. PEPM ’20.&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3372884.3373159&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3372884.3373159&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 44px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font&gt;Acknowledgements&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;Mention OGS and NSERC?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="800" width="900" x="2600" y="1500" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="U_MLOzHVXz4xIFYg9_O6-4" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;spacingLeft=0;spacingTop=0;spacing=50;fontFamily=Poppins;fillColor=default;strokeColor=default;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 44px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font&gt;Relation to Visibility&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;On top of pure organization, these &quot;organizational structures&quot; are also used to control which names (variables, functions, types, etc.) are accessible from other &quot;organizational structures&quot;. The semantics of this also varies between languages, so we need to make sure we translate visibility management in a correct and idiomatic manner. If a language&#39;s vocabulary cannot express what we want to express safely (i.e. cannot prevent a name collision or cannot make one name reachable from a structure that needs it), then we should detect this and throw an error.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="800" width="900" x="2600" y="600" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="DqRWUP40LE4QbgxWnG_u-6" parent="1" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;shapeInside=1;fontSize=30;fontFamily=Poppins;fillColor=#CCFFCC;" value="Level 0" vertex="1">
